Project Title

Data Cleaning and Preprocessing Analysis

Objective

The objective of this project is to clean and preprocess raw datasets by handling missing values, removing duplicates, standardizing data, and detecting outliers to improve data quality and reliability.

Dataset

The datasets contain raw data with:

Missing values
Duplicate records
Inconsistent formatting
Outliers
Tools and Libraries Used
Python
Pandas
NumPy
Matplotlib
Seaborn
Jupyter Notebook
Steps Performed
1. Data Loading
Imported datasets using Pandas.
2. Data Exploration
Viewed dataset structure
Checked data types and summary information
3. Missing Value Handling
Identified missing values
Filled missing numerical values using mean
Filled categorical values using mode
4. Duplicate Removal
Detected duplicate rows
Removed duplicate records
5. Data Standardization
Converted text into consistent formatting
Removed extra spaces and inconsistencies
6. Outlier Detection
Used IQR (Interquartile Range) method
Identified extreme values in numerical columns
7. Outlier Removal
Removed detected outliers for cleaner analysis
8. Final Clean Dataset
Generated cleaned datasets ready for analysis and machine learning tasks
Key Insights
Missing and duplicate data can affect analysis accuracy.
Standardization improves consistency across datasets.
Outlier handling improves overall data reliability.
Outcome

This project improved understanding of:

Data preprocessing
Data quality management
Missing value handling
Outlier detection techniques
Data cleaning workflows
Conclusion

The project successfully cleaned and standardized raw datasets by handling inconsistencies, duplicates, missing values, and outliers, resulting in high-quality datasets suitable for further analysis.